      "admission": "ADDENDUM 6 \u00a76.1: a component is admitted on its sealed frozen-review verdict, not on free-run token match, which the addendum retires to a diagnostic column.",
      "block_exclusivity": "NOTES-MX-K \u00a72.1: a block hosts at most one folded LANE.  The operator lane (short_conv / full_attention) writes operator.output upstream of the block's FFN norm; the feed-forward lane reads that norm.  Folding both in one block solves the MLP against a residual the operator fold has already moved -- measured at -3 review cases for mlp_gate and -4 for mlp_down against the same block's conv writer, while the two MLP tensors together in one block cost nothing.  Two components in the SAME lane are therefore allowed; two lanes are refused.",
      "install_order": "topological, input side -> output side; within a layer conv -> attention -> mlp -> norms (matrix_composition.install_order_key)",
      "ranking": "greedy, block-exclusive; a rung is kept only if the composed child stays alive-degraded or better (>= 8/15) and is not dead by the degeneracy clause",
      "site_scope": "ADDENDUM 5 rule 2-S under ADDENDUM 7's widened registry: a site that schema v2 registers has NO evidence attached to it by being registered.  Every rung is measured or it is nothing.",
